<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n46737" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἠερο-ειδής</span></b> , <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ές</span>, 
			Ion.
		and 
			Ep.
		 for <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀερ-</span>, which is not
		found, <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>misty, cloudy, dark</i>
			(esp. in <i><span class="en">
				Od.
			</span></i>), 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἐπ᾽ ἠεροειδέα πόντον</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Od.
					2.263
				</span></i>
			, etc.; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">σπέος ἠ</span>. <i><span class="en">
				12.80
			</span></i>, cf. <i><span class="en">
				13.103
			</span></i>; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">πέτρη</span>, of
			Scylla&lt;*&gt;s cave, <i><span class="en">
				12.233
			</span></i>: neut. as Adv., <i>in the far distance,
			dimly</i>, 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ὅσσον δ᾽ ἠεροειδὲς ἀνὴρ ἴδεν</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Il.
					5.770
				</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἠ. νεφέλη</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Hes.
					<u>Th.</u>
					757
				</span></i>
			; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">πνοιαί</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Orph.
					<u>H.</u>
					38.22
				</span></i>
			.—
				Ep.
			 word, 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἠ. αὐγαί</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Arist.
					<u>Col.</u>
					792b8
				</span></i>
			: 
				Comp.
			, 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ὕδωρ πάντων -έστερον</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Arr.
					<u>Ind.</u>
					6.3
				</span></i>
			.</div>
